                            <div class="tab-pane show active" id="screenshots">
                                <section class="oe_container mt48" style="background-color: transparent !important;">
                                  <section class="oe_container mt32 mb32 " style="background-color: transparent !important;">
                                   
                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Upon installing the module, you can see the Forecast application.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="1.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">You can define as many forecast rules as you wish. A Forecast Rule is configured for a warehouse & company with product selection, 
                                    defining forecast period, demand calculation method, supply planning parameters, and warehouse transfer settings to automate stock planning and replenishment.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <ul>
                                        <li><p><b>Rule Name:</b>Enter a unique name for the forecast rule.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Company:</b>You have to define for which company you want to do the forecast for.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Warehouse:</b>If you have multiple warehouse in the same company, you can define which warehouse needs forecasting and auto replenishment.</p></li>                                    
                                        <li><p><b>Product Selection:</b> You can select products based on product templates, product category and vendor.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Forecast Days:</b> Number of future days to get the forecasting quantities.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Sale History Days:</b> Number of past days to consider for sales history analysis.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Forecast Methods:</b> You can choose to forecast based on daily, monthly and same period last year calculation methods.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Lead Time Days:</b> Number of days required to receive stock after placing an order.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Safety Stock Days:</b> Extra stock buffer (in days) maintained to avoid shortages during demand fluctuations.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Order Cycle Days:</b> It defines how often you order for selected products.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Reorder Rules:</b> You can choose to enter the minimum quantity to order and order multiple in the rule, or use the existing reorder rules for the product.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Minimum Reorder Quantity:</b> Minimum quantity that must be ordered in a purchase order.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Reorder Multiple:</b> Quantity must be ordered in multiples of this value.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Maximum Stock Limit:</b> Maximum stock limit for the selected warehouse.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Source Warehouse:</b> You can add multiple source warehouses and maintain their priority for internal transfer from those warehouses to the current warehouse.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Operation Type:</b> You can choose the operation type to create in Odoo for internal transfer.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Source Required Quantity:</b> Minimum quantity required in the source warehouse.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Minimum Transfer Quantity:</b> Ensures a minimum quantity is used for transfers.</p></li>
                                    </ul>

                                    <img src="2.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    

                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Each seasonality rule allows to set month-wise demand factors to manage forecast based on seasonal trends.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="3.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    <img src="4.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">


                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">This is the scheduled action to generate product forecast lines.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="5.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    


                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Product forecasts are displayed by grouping items into In Stock and Shortages.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="6.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    <img src="7.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    

                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Detailed view of each product forecast includes several information. 
                                    </p>       
                                    <ul>
                                        <li><p><b>Forecast Rule:</b> Forecast rule used to forecast this product's quantity.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Warehouse:</b> Warehouse for the forecasted product.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Sold Quantity:</b> Shows the sold quantities for the time period used for data analysis.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Action Type:</b> What you require to fulfill the shortage quantity.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Action Summary:</b> Whether you need to transfer quantities from another warehouse or create a purchase order for this product with the exact quantity.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Forecast Period:</b> This forecast is calculated for this specific period.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Forecasted Quantity:</b> Actual forecasted quantity for the product based on the configuration in the forecasting rule.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Shortage Quantity:</b> Shortage quantity based on the current net stock and forecasted quantity.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Forecast Calculation:</b> Shows the exact calculation for the forecasted quantity for your reference.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Average Daily Demand:</b> Shows the average daily demand based on the sold quantity.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Lead Time Demand:</b> Shows the demand during the lead time days.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Order Cycle Demand:</b> Shows the forecasted quantity required for the order cycle days.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Safety Stock:</b> Shows the safety stock based on the safety stock days configuration in the rule.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Net Stock:</b> Shows the current net stock.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b>Vendor:</b> You can choose the vendor in case a purchase order needs to be created.</p></li>
                                    </ul>                             
                                    <img src="8.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">

                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">This scheduled action automatically runs the transfer process generating internal transfers and/or purchase orders based on action summary.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="9.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">

                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Tracks each automated or manual transfer/order with details.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="10.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">

                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Each log line contains details of transfers and/or purchase orders.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="11.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">


                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Shows the internal transfer & purchase order created from the schedule action/manual run transfer button.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="12.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    <img src="13.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">


                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Deadstock Report shows recent movement to categorize products into Active, Slow Moving, Very Slow Moving, and Deadstock.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="14.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    <img src="15.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">

                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Fast Moving Report analyzes recent product movement and classifies items as Fast, Medium, or Slow Moving based on their sales trend.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="16.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    <img src="17.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">


                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Excess Stock Report identifies products where current stock exceeds the required forecast level stock, highlighting overstock situations.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="18.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">


                                    <p style="text-align: left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 20px; 
                                        padding-bottom: 10px;">
                                    <img src="./img/aerrow.png" class="img img-fluid">Days of Inventory Report shows products where stock will last longer than the target period days, indicating potential overstock based on coverage days.
                                    </p>                                    
                                    <img src="19.png" class="img img-fluid shadow" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                                    
                                    
                                   

                                    
                                  </section>
                                </section>
